==German==

===Etymology===
{{root|de|ine-pro|*(s)kreybʰ-}}
From {{inh|de|gmh|schrift}}, from {{inh|de|goh|scrift}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*skrifti|t=writing, scripture}}, from {{der|de|la|scriptum}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ʃʁɪft/}}
* {{audio|de|De-Schrift.oga}}
* {{rhymes|de|ɪft}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f}}

# [[writing]], [[script]]
#: {{ux|de|Wir wissen nicht, ob es sich bei diesen Zeichen um '''Schrift''' oder magische Symbole handelt.|We do not know whether these characters are '''writing''' or magical symbols.}}
#: {{ux|de|Jegliche Änderungen dieser Verträge bedürfen der '''Schrift'''form.|Any changes to these contracts must be made in '''writing'''.}}
# [[script]] {{gloss|system of writing}}
#: {{syn|de|Schriftsystem}}
#: {{uxi|de|die chinesische '''Schrift'''|the Chinese '''script'''}}
# [[hand]], [[handwriting]] {{gloss|individual way of drawing characters}}
#: {{syn|de|Handschrift|Hand}}
#: {{uxi|de|Er hat eine ordentliche '''Schrift'''.|He has a neat '''handwriting'''.}}
# [[font]] {{gloss|specific design of printed characters}}
#: {{syn|de|Schriftart|q2=rare or specialist|Font}}
#: {{ux|de|Verdana ist die beste '''Schrift''' zur Bildschirmbetrachtung.|Verdana is the best '''font''' for viewing on the computer screen.}}
# {{lb|de|often|in the plural}} [[writing]], [[text]] {{gloss|work of an author}}
#: {{syn|de|Text|Werk}}
#: {{ux|de|Robert Oppenheimer las Lenins gesammelte '''Schriften''' während einer Zugfahrt.|Robert Oppenheimer read the complete '''writings''' of Lenin while on a train.}}
# [[scripture]] {{gloss|holy text}}
#: {{ux|de|In vielen Religionen ist das Verhältnis von '''Schrift''' und Tradition strittig.|The relation between '''scripture''' and tradition is a matter of debate in many religions.}}

